%[text] %[text:anchor:T_C4C9F2AF] # Programming: A Starter Project Using MATLAB with Python
%[text:tableOfContents]{"heading":"Table of Contents"}
openProject("MATLABwithPython.prj"); %[text:anchor:H_4F193DCD]
  %[control:button:2f55]{"position":[1,2]}
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_315D4D54] ## Scripts
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_8CD26475] ### [UsingMATLABwithPython.m](file:Scripts/UsingMATLABwithPython.m) 
%[text:table]{"columnWidths":[-1,575]}
%[text] | **Introductory script** | **In this script, students will...** |
%[text] | --- | --- |
%[text] | ![Run Python Live Task](text:image:44f2) | <p></p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"bullet"} check that an appropriate version of Python is installed and visible within MATLAB</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"bullet"} explore the Run Python Code Live Task</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"bullet"} try running Python commands and a Python script from MATLAB</p><p></p> |
%[text:table]
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_0B917A5E] ### [CheckingTheWeather.m](file:Scripts/CheckingTheWeather.m) 
%[text:table]{"columnWidths":[-1,575]}
%[text] | **Investigatory script** | **In this script, students will...** |
%[text] | --- | --- |
%[text] | ![a screenshot of the creation of a struct with both MATLAB and Python data types](text:image:7698) | <p></p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"bullet"} set up an account with OpenWeather to create your own API key</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"bullet"} use existing Python code to make an API call to OpenWeather</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"bullet"} use MATLAB to explore the data returned by the API call, including data type conversions and unit conversions</p> |
%[text:table]
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_38A57F9E] ### [CreateCurrentWeatherApp.m](file:Scripts/CreateCurrentWeatherApp.m) 
%[text:table]{"columnWidths":[-1,575]}
%[text] | **Application script** | **In this script, students will...** |
%[text] | --- | --- |
%[text] | ![Current Weather App screenshot](text:image:92d3) | <p></p><p></p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"bullet"} use App Designer to build a custom app using the code from CheckingTheWeather.m</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"bullet"} create callbacks, properties, and functions</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"bullet"} design and organize a UI with drag and drop elements</p><p>$\\bullet${"altText":"bullet"} reuse code from CheckingTheWeather in a new context</p> |
%[text:table]
%%
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_C37314C3] ## Apps
%[text] Both of these apps require running Python from MATLAB, as set up in [UsingMATLABwithPython](internal:H_8CD26475) and an OpenWeather API key, as set up in [CheckingTheWeather](internal:H_0B917A5E).
%[text] The Current Weather App Demo shows the results of working through CreateCurrentWeatherApp. 
  %[control:button:8043]{"position":[1,2]}
CurrentWeatherAppDemo 
%%
  %[control:button:0d26]{"position":[1,2]}
open CurrentWeatherAppDemo.mlapp
%%
%[text] The Weather Display app shows one elaborated version of the basic current weather app. 
  %[control:button:6d3a]{"position":[1,2]}
WeatherDisplay 
%%
  %[control:button:9f87]{"position":[1,2]}
open WeatherDisplay.mlapp
